# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Icequake_ML .gitignore
#
# The repository tracks CODE, DOCUMENTATION and a curated set of RESULTS
# (full_catalog_pipeline/figures/ and full_catalog_pipeline/tables/). It does
# NOT track the generated data tree, which is ~31 GB, nor the external
# datasets, which are large and separately archived.
#
# If you need to regenerate anything, see full_catalog_pipeline/README.md for
# which script produces which artifact.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- generated data tree (~31 GB): waveform windows, per-run hypoDD trees,
#     per-cluster diagnostics, 883 figures, 372 CSVs -------------------------
full_catalog_pipeline/artifacts/
# ...but keep the curated handoff results, which live outside artifacts/:
!full_catalog_pipeline/figures/
!full_catalog_pipeline/tables/

# --- external datasets: download separately, see METHODS.md §2 and §9 -------
# CATS2008_v2023.nc: 1.7 GB ocean tide model, USAP-DC dataset 601772 (CC BY 4.0)
CATS2008_v2023.nc
# gps_data/: processed GPS, from jakewalter.mynetgear.com:~/gps/
gps_data/
# easyquake_project/: 97 MB easyQuake working tree
easyquake_project/

# --- per-run training outputs from the SNR ablation (§3): metadata tables up to
#     24 MB each, plus their model checkpoints. Regenerate with 01_dataset/ + 02_picker/.
full_catalog_pipeline/output/
full_catalog_pipeline/output_[A-E]/
full_catalog_pipeline/checkpoints/
full_catalog_pipeline/checkpoints_[A-E]/
full_catalog_pipeline/rpnet_model/

# --- ML training data and model weights ------------------------------------
final_curated_seisbench_data/waveforms.hdf5
*.pth
*.h5
*.hdf5

# NOTE: full_catalog_pipeline/vels1d/ (28 KB, the MEASURED reflection velocity profile) IS
# tracked deliberately — vels1d_model.py reads it and the whole relocation stage depends on it.

# --- manuscript drafts and their Word conversions --------------------------
# docs/ holds paper-facing prose (METHODS_paper.md, METHODS_summary.md), the .docx
# conversions, and superseded drafts. Deliberately NOT tracked: manuscript text belongs in
# whatever the writing workflow is (Word/Overleaf), not versioned here, and .docx is an opaque
# binary that git cannot diff. The internal record METHODS.md at the repository root IS
# tracked and is the source these are generated from:
#     python -c "import pypandoc; pypandoc.convert_file('METHODS.md','docx',
#         outputfile='docs/METHODS.docx', extra_args=['--from=gfm+pipe_tables','--toc'])"
docs/

# --- scratch, logs, caches -------------------------------------------------
# hypoDD experimental reruns (catalog_paths.scratch_dir); trimmed inputs + raw hypoDD
# output, regenerable by rerunning the script that made them.
full_catalog_pipeline/scratch/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.log
hypoDD.log
inspect_raw_probs.out
